  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 202 AM MDT MON SEP 7 2026\nThe warm, dry weather will continue Thursday with high temps \nwell into the 80s in the lower valleys and 75 to 85 degrees \nin the mountains. Later Thursday a new upper trough will dig \nsouthward along the BC coast. The trough will push a dry surface\ncold front southeastward through our CWA Thursday night. The \nfront will bring gusty winds from the west or northwest, \nfollowed by cooler, breezy weather Friday through Sunday, with \nSunday likely as cool as today. The supporting upper trough \nwill bring a chance of showers to our northern mountain zones \nSaturday and Sunday, with snow level near 8000 feet.",
